a new version of this parcelable. In order to make sure your code continues to be backwards compatible, make sure the default or null value does not cause a semantic change to this parcelable.\nERROR: hardware/interfaces/bluetooth/audio/aidl/aidl_api/android.hardware.bluetooth.audio/current/android/hardware/bluetooth/audio/LeAudioCodecConfiguration.aidl:39.63-84: Field \u0027aptxadaptiveleConfig\u0027 does not have a useful default in some backends. Please either provide a default value for this field or mark the field as @nullable. This value or a null value will be used automatically when an old version of this parcelable is sent to a process which understands a new version of this parcelable. In order to make sure your code continues to be backwards compatible, make sure the default or null value does not cause a semantic change to this parcelable.\n###############################################################################\n# ERROR: Backward incompatible change detected on AIDL API                    #\n###############################################################################\nAbove AIDL file(s) has changed in a backward-incompatible way, e.g. removing\na method from an interface or a field from a parcelable. If a device is shipped\nwith this change by ignoring this message, it has a high risk of breaking later\nwhen a module using the interface is updated, e.g., Maineline modules.\n07:57:47 ninja failed with: exit status 1\n\n_________________________________________________________________________________\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nMoreover, it seems when AIDL was Rev-up for V2 with OPUS codec addition. \nOPUS structure was also made nullable for that reason only.\nMay be Steven can confirm more on this from an interface version compatibility viewpoint.\n \nhttps://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:hardware/interfaces/bluetooth/audio/aidl/android/hardware/bluetooth/audio/CodecConfiguration.aidl;bpv\u003d0\n\n    union CodecSpecific {\n     