      "writtenOn": "2023-02-14T23:50:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Would there be room just for one LTV value, or do we want to allow multiple LTV values?\n\nIn the BT spec, multiple LTVs are allowed and hence I think we should just say this is a standard Bluetooth LTV format\n\nWe already have a similar byte array in \n\nhttps://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:packages/modules/Bluetooth/framework/java/android/bluetooth/BluetoothLeAudioCodecConfigMetadata.java;l\u003d181\n\nIf you are using the same LTV from the Generic Audio assigned numbers, should you just copy the documentation from the above java API?\n\nOr if the metadata is defined else where, could you provide link to the public documentation of this metadata from the Bluetooth SIG website? and cite which version, section, and/or page number is the definition located \n\nOtherwise, LGTM on this byte array",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 48,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 54,
        "endChar": 7
      },
      "revId": "9fd61c28cb3596676a03cc912d99d163d0dda3cf",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fe813393_2804bfe1",
        "filename": "bluetooth/audio/aidl/android/hardware/bluetooth/audio/LeAudioConfiguration.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 54,
      "author": {
        "id": 1312909
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-15T08:40:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Q1. Would there be room just for one LTV value, or do we want to allow multiple LTV values?\n\n\u003cSagar\u003e Theoretically using byte array multiple LTV is possible. \nBut as the name and description suggests it\u0027s meant for vendor specific metadata (type - 0xFF).\nBT Spec is having provision of sending vendor metadata as shared over mail in LE Generic Audio section.\nhttps://btprodspecificationrefs.blob.core.windows.net/assigned-numbers/Assigned%20Number%20Types/Generic%20Audio.pdf\n\nRegarding multi-LTV query, currently we are planning for one single LTV only for given LeAudioConfiguration. But in future, if any particular vendor wants to send more LTV it can send it in single LTV itself in a nested format as below,\n\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nOctet      |     Name               |             Value            \n0          |     Length             |      Variable (Overall length)\n1          |     Type               |      0xFF - Vendor Specific Metadata\n2-3        |     Company ID         |       0x000A - Qualcomm (example)\n4          |     VS Metadata length |      LTV length octet (L say length)\n5          |     VS Metadata type   |      LTV type octet\n6 to L+4   |     VS Metadata value  |      LTV value octet(s)\nL+5        |     Next LTV           |      Additional LTV (if needed)\n_________________________________________________________________________________\n*VS - vendor specific\n________________________________________________________________________________\n\nRemote can send PACS vendor Metadata in above format (more LTV) which will be passed on to codec via AIDL.\n\nI don\u0027t see any scenario where for same LE session config anyone will update multi LTV of two different vendors while single vendor multi LTV scenario can be covered using above nested LTV structures.\n\n\nQ2. We already have a similar byte array in\n\nhttps://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:packages/modules/Bluetooth/framework/java/android/bluetooth/BluetoothLeAudioCodecConfigMetadata.java;l\u003d181\n\nIf you are using the same LTV from the Generic Audio assigned numbers, should you just copy the documentation from the above java API?\n\n\u003cSagar\u003e I am not very sure about its current usage in AOSP it can be open for all types of LTVs (standard and vendor both). However, in our byte array we are only targeting for vendor specific metadata only while Java one seems more generic.",
      "parentUuid": "9a0f4d38_4e86b526",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 48,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 54,
        "endChar": 7
      },
      "revId": "9fd61c28cb3596676a03cc912d99d163d0dda3cf",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
